<p>
    <strong>Core Gameplan:</strong> Monitor opposing land acceleration
    closely for <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Weathered Wayfarer"
        >Weathered Wayfarer</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Sylvan Library">Sylvan Library</a
    >, and impending <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Armageddon">Armageddon</a
    > resolutions. Having a disciplined tactical plan for Armageddon
    does not necessarily mean stopping it on the stack: withholding
    basic lands in hand after reaching three mana is an exceptional
    strategic defense. Alternatively, resolving an early <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    > to establish dominant board pressure makes casting Armageddon
    an active suicide play for the opponent.
</p>
<p>
    <strong>Sideboard Strategy:</strong> Trim bulky combo infrastructure
    (<a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Parallax Wave">Parallax Wave</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Opalescence">Opalescence</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Attunement">Attunement</a
    >) and excise all copies of <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Meddling Mage">Meddling Mage</a
    >. Bring in <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Exalted Angel">Exalted Angel</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Seal of Cleansing">Seal of Cleansing</a
    >, <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Arcane Denial">Arcane Denial</a
    >, and <a
        href="#"
        class="card-hover"
        data-card-name="Tsabo's Web">Tsabo's Web</a
    >.
</p>
